      "description": "The IG site pipeline's code and the Liquid templates it renders with: `stage-ig-sites.ts` stages each instance's IG as its own just-the-docs site, `build-ig-site.ts` turns an IG's `input/` and `sushi-config.yaml` into that site (navigation, colour scheme, the lifted `site.data.fhir` artefact variables, and the Publisher-generated pages `toc` and `artifacts`), `ig-site-data.ts` lifts the IG's `_data`, and `ig-ast.ts` lists, checks, diffs and renders IG ASTs. Templates sit under `templates/`, beside the writer that reads them (`liquid-templates`). Undeclared until 2026-10-01 while the Tool nodes in `tools/` invoked every one of these files: a `.liquid` file in an undeclared directory is one no checker looks at, which is what declaring it fixes.",
